  "result": "`split(cents, parts)` is added to `shop/money.py` with tests in `tests/test_money.py`, and the suite passes. I could not run `pytest`, so the tests ran under `unittest`.\n\n```python\ndef split(cents: int, parts: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Split cents into parts; the remainder goes one cent at a time from the front.\"\"\"\n    if parts < 1:\n        raise ValueError(f\"parts must be at least 1: {parts}\")\n    base, extra = divmod(cents, parts)\n    return [base + 1 if i < extra else base for i in range(parts)]\n```\n\nThe new tests cover:\n- Remainder spread from the front, e.g. `split(10, 3)` gives `[4, 3, 3]` and `split(7, 4)` gives `[2, 2, 2, 1]`.\n- An even split.\n- The sum equals `cents`.\n- `ValueError` for `parts=0` and for a negative `parts`.\n\nI wrote the tests in `unittest` style to match `tests/test_pricing.py`. Command: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`. Result: 11 tests ran, all OK.\n\n`python` is not on PATH and `pytest` is not installed for `python3`, so `pytest -q` was not run. Nothing was committed.",
